WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.920
Ray Stevenson had a varied acting career,&nbsp;
but arguably his highest-profile roles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.460
were linked to Marvel. He made a&nbsp;
strong impression not only on fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.720
but also on the people he worked with on&nbsp;
those films. They spoke up to memorialize him.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.300
On May 22, 2023, news of Stevenson's&nbsp;
death at the age of 58 came as a shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.200
to fans all over the world. His death&nbsp;
reportedly occurred a day earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.380
and as of the making of this video,&nbsp;
the cause has yet to be made public.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.700
Stevenson turned in numerous memorable&nbsp;
performances on screens big and small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.400
throughout his acting career,&nbsp;
entertaining moviegoers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.300
television viewers alike in a wide range&nbsp;
of genres. But Marvel fans, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.560
best remember his work under the Marvel&nbsp;
banner, within the MCU and outside of it.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.180
Stevenson's first Marvel role came in&nbsp;
2008 as the title character in "Punisher:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.680
War Zone," a gory and grim take on Frank&nbsp;
Castle's story that's all too often overlooked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.180
during discussions of Punisher adaptations.&nbsp;
Sadly, this turned out to be Stevenson's only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.020
live-action turn in the role, but he'd get&nbsp;
another crack at a Marvel character a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.760
years later. In 2011's "Thor," he took on&nbsp;
the role of Warriors Three member Volstagg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.224
which he reprised in the 2013 sequel "Thor:&nbsp;
The Dark World" and 2017's "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:01:08.224 --> 00:01:12.120
"My friends! This is good!"

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.280
As word of Stevenson's death has spread,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.300
folks that have worked in front of and behind&nbsp;
the camera for Marvel productions made touching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.380
statements on social media in his memory.&nbsp;
James Gunn, director of the "Guardians of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.340
the Galaxy" trilogy and holiday special,&nbsp;
and now the co-head of DC Studios, wrote,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.720
"So sorry to hear about the passing, far&nbsp;
too young, of Ray Stevenson. I only knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.620
him a little from shooting post-credits of&nbsp;
Thor 2 &amp; a couple interactions at events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.420
but we had some good laughs &amp; he was a joy to work&nbsp;
with. His friends &amp; family are in my heart today."

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.620
Rosario Dawson, who played Claire Temple&nbsp;
on the Netflix Marvel series "Daredevil"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.720
and "Luke Cage," also posted a Twitter tribute to&nbsp;
Stevenson, calling him "vivacious &amp; unbelievably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.820
present &amp; vibrant." Dawson and Stevenson worked&nbsp;
extensively on the upcoming Disney+ "Star Wars"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.720
series "Ahsoka," which will arrive on&nbsp;
the streaming service in August 2023.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.700
Stevenson's work as the fallen Jedi Baylan Skoll&nbsp;
on the program is one of his final performances.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.840
Stevenson was remembered well by his&nbsp;
fellow Warriors Three actors. On Instagram,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.180
Tadanobu Asano, who played Hogun, reminisced&nbsp;
about their time working together. Asano described&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.980
Stevenson's kindness, helpfulness, and warmth, and&nbsp;
thanked him for all he did for him. Josh Dallas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.180
who played Fandral in the first "Thor" movie&nbsp;
before Zachary Levi took over the role in "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.500
The Dark World" and "Thor: Ragnarok," posted&nbsp;
about Stevenson on his Instagram story, writing,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.880
"Rest in peace Ray."

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.660
Jaimie Alexander, who has played Lady&nbsp;
Sif in a number of Marvel productions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.380
shared some photos of herself and&nbsp;
Stevenson on set. She began her caption,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.820
"Ray. Man. My heart is shattered.&nbsp;
You made everyday so much fun on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.120
and off set. You always looked&nbsp;
after me. Always made me laugh."

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.080
Alexander recalled Stevenson visiting her&nbsp;
in the hospital and their unforgettable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.780
dinners. Though she had plenty&nbsp;
of stories to share about him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.500
she wished they had the chance to make&nbsp;
even more memories. She concluded her post,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.740
"I'm sending so much love to&nbsp;
your beautiful family. Love you."

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.160
Just as he did with fans of his&nbsp;
work, Ray Stevenson clearly left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.240
a lasting impression on many of his&nbsp;
co-stars. He is already sorely missed.

